v850: do not share the parent's vmlist with a cloned mm

dup_mm() memcpy()s the parent's mm_struct for a clone without CLONE_VM,
and on 2.6.26 noMMU the list of memory regions lives in
mm->context.vmlist.  init_new_context() left it alone, so the child
pointed at the parent's list and exit_mmap() freed the parent's entries
and dropped the usage count of its regions when the child exited.
The parent then ran on freed memory (test/unistd/clone hung).

Start the child with an empty vmlist, like newer noMMU kernels do.

diff -Nur linux-2.6.26.orig/include/asm-v850/mmu_context.h linux-2.6.26/include/asm-v850/mmu_context.h
--- linux-2.6.26.orig/include/asm-v850/mmu_context.h	2026-11-21 11:59:21.273422235 +0100
+++ linux-2.6.26/include/asm-v850/mmu_context.h	2026-11-21 11:59:21.280944762 +0100
@@ -4,7 +4,9 @@
 #include <asm-generic/mm_hooks.h>
 
 #define destroy_context(mm)		((void)0)
-#define init_new_context(tsk,mm)	0
+/* A clone without CLONE_VM gets a copy of the parent's mm_struct; do not
+   let it inherit (and free on exit) the parent's vmlist.  */
+#define init_new_context(tsk,mm)	((mm)->context.vmlist = NULL, 0)
 #define switch_mm(prev,next,tsk)	((void)0)
 #define deactivate_mm(tsk,mm)		do { } while (0)
 #define activate_mm(prev,next)		((void)0)
